                            <comment id="14220799" author="ikelly" created="Fri, 21 Nov 2014 11:38:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fix is to check each write quorum after each response. If there is no write quorum with |ackQuorum| nodes available, then it is not possible for a writer to form a quorum without at least one of the nodes we have heard a response from.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14220801" author="ikelly" created="Fri, 21 Nov 2014 11:40:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://reviews.apache.org/r/28326/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://reviews.apache.org/r/28326/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14220866" author="fpj" created="Fri, 21 Nov 2014 12:57:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Good catch! Write quorums are defined in a round-robin fashion so there is no gap in the sequence of ordered server ids for a write quorum, but since an ack quorum can be a subset of a write quorum, an ack quorum might have gaps in the sequence of bookies ids.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14220892" author="ikelly" created="Fri, 21 Nov 2014 13:22:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think that once this is in we should roll a 4.2.4 and 4.3.1 release. I&apos;d like to wait until TLP stuff is set up first though. Branches are much easier to deal with in git.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
